Omarchy background renderer adaptation

Source: https://github.com/basecamp/omarchy-site
Pinned commit: 2af2bcdc41c1eba20a2f4d6a98b9521f5d014dc8
Source component: HeroPixelField.tsx
Companion reference: music.ts (BANDS = 32)

web/background.mjs directly adapts HeroPixelField's seeded two-pass smoothed
noise, jitter tile, smooth sampling, 8x8 Bayer thresholding, drifting field
luminance, pointer reach and easing, mirrored spectrum columns, colour heat
selection, square-spiral logo bitmap and quick-click stamp growth/dissolution.

The React wrapper, site wordmark, etching, theme picker, autonomous sprite,
audio loading/playback and silent music timeline are omitted. Canvas layout
uses a bounded viewport grid instead of the site wordmark grid. Application
palette colours supply the inks. Reduced motion is stationary; hidden views
suspend updates. Ten captured music bands are interpolated into the source's
32 visual columns, with a three-second capture/receive freshness guard.
The source beat envelope accepts only explicitly supplied captured beat data;
no silent timeline, generated beats or autoplay are included. Input currently
without beat data supplies zero beat energy. Clicks use the source's zero-charge
launch because the application API does not expose press-and-hold duration.

